{"created": "2026-10-17T20:44:08.320820+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-17T20:44:08.762545+00:00", "id": 23441906, "conceptrecid": "23441905", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23441906", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23441905", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23441906", "metadata": {"title": "A simple brace outside asymmetric products of two trivial braces", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23441906", "publication_date": "2026-10-17", "description": "<p>A full negative answer to Cedo Problem 9 in Oberwolfach Report 51/2019, printed p.3228 (problem 30004311; OWR-17294-011). An explicit nontrivial simple left brace of order 20,000 has additive group C5^4 x C2^5 and metabelian multiplicative group (C5^3 semidirect C2) x (C2^4 semidirect C5), with all multiplicative Sylow subgroups abelian. It is not an asymmetric product of two trivial braces.</p><p>The five-page research note gives all operations, the group isomorphism, a proof covering every nonzero ideal, and a universal presentation-independent obstruction. Under the full admissible normalized symmetric-cocycle definition, such two-factor products with abelian multiplicative Sylow subgroups have zero primary triple star products. The example instead has (x*x)*x = x^3 nonzero in its 5-primary subbrace. Established radical-ring, matched-product, asymmetric-product, truncated logarithm and cyclic orthogonal methods are credited; no new general construction formalism is claimed. The source archive retains the original proof, three independently authored mathematical audits, extensive current priority and implication audits, four unchanged standard-library verification programs, exact results and per-seed certificates. Finite computation supplements the universal written proofs.</p><p>A bounded primary-source audit on 17 October 2026 identified no prior full answer or verified prior full implication; exhaustive priority and historical novelty are uncertified. The full bodies of Rump 2020 and 2022 and several final journal versions, including the 2025 Cedo-Okni\u0144ski paper, were unavailable. Broader consequences are not excluded by abstracts. Citation coverage and the query-defined recent arXiv screen are incomplete; all inspection boundaries are documented. AI tools were used extensively in construction, proof development, computation, adversarial verification, literature research and writing. Unrefereed; AI adversarial reviews are not external human peer review, journal acceptance or formal proof-assistant certification.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["left brace", "simple brace", "asymmetric product", "metabelian group", "abelian Sylow subgroups", "Yang-Baxter equation", "Cedo Problem 9"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.4171/OWR/2019/51", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/46831", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.1016/j.jalgebra.2016.01.038", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.08493v1", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.4171/rmi/1168", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.08905v1", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.12904v2", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.01884v2", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.20401v1", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.24640v1", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1121", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype